# Global Agent Instructions

These instructions apply across coding agents and projects.

## General Guidelines

- Read a file before editing it.
  Do not propose code changes without inspecting the relevant code.
- When writing or substantially editing long Markdown files, put each full sentence on its own physical line.
- Prefer quality, simplicity, correctness, robustness, and long-term maintainability over development speed.
- Simplification is mandatory.
  Remove dead code, speculative flexibility, and premature generalization.
- Solve root causes instead of layering patches over symptoms.
- Match existing project patterns unless there is a strong technical reason to change them.
- Do not introduce dependencies, abstractions, services, or infrastructure without a concrete current requirement.
- Preserve type safety.
  Avoid unchecked casts, broad exception handling, and silent fallbacks that hide invalid states.
- Never add an AI product, company, model, agent name, or AI identity as a commit co-author.
- Treat third-party skills as executable instructions.
  Inspect them before installation and prefer trusted, auditable sources.

## Bug Fixes

- Reproduce meaningful bugs as closely as possible to the end-user path.
- Trace the failure to its root cause before implementing a fix.
- Add a regression test whenever the failure can reasonably be automated.
- Verify the original reproduction path after the fix.

## Engineering Quality

- Treat lint failures, type errors, test failures, flaky tests, security regressions, and build failures as defects.
- Test behavior users experience, not only implementation details.
- Leave the codebase simpler and more reliable than you found it.

## Environment

- OS: fill in yours, e.g. Windows 11.
- Follow the path syntax of the active shell.
  In Git Bash, use `/c/dev/` paths rather than `C:\dev\` paths.

## Workflow

For non-trivial work: `plan -> implement -> finalize`.
Apply relevant skills by intent even when runtimes expose different invocation syntax.
Do not bypass review or tests merely to save time.
